msgid "Communicating to the backend"
msgstr ""

msgid "JsonRPC against the Runtime classpath"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can fetch or stream runtime data (rather than <<Build time data>> "
"discussed earlier) or execute methods against the runtime classpath (as "
"opposed to deployment classpath). There are two parts to getting data during "
"runtime. The Java side in the runtime module, and then the usage in the web "
"component."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Java part*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This code is responsible for making data available to display on the UI."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You must register the `JsonPRCService` in your processor in the deployment "
"module:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Always only do this in Dev Mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "Produce or return a `JsonRPCProvidersBuildItem`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Define the class in your runtime module that will contain methods that make "
"data available in the UI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/main/extensions/cache/deployment/"
"src/main/java/io/quarkus/cache/deployment/devui/CacheDevUiProcessor."
"java[Example code]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now, in your Runtime module, create the JsonRPC Service. This class will "
"default to an application-scoped bean, except if you explicitly scope the "
"bean. All public methods that return something will be made available to "
"call from the Web component Javascript."
msgstr ""

msgid "The return object in these methods can be:"
msgstr ""

msgid "primitives or `String`,"
msgstr ""

msgid "`io.vertx.core.json.JsonArray`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`io.vertx.core.json.JsonObject`"
msgstr ""

msgid "any other POJO that can be serializable to JSON"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All of the above can be blocking (POJO) or nonblocking (`@NonBlocking` or "
"`Uni`). Alternatively, data can be streamed using `Multi`."
msgstr ""

msgid "This example runs nonblocking. We could also return `Uni<JsonArray>`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The method name `getAll` will be available in the Javascript"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/main/extensions/cache/runtime/src/"
"main/java/io/quarkus/cache/runtime/devui/CacheJsonRPCService.java[Example "
"code]"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Webcomponent (Javascript) part*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now you can use the JsonRPC controller to access the `getAll` method (and "
"any other methods in your JsonRPC Service)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note the method `getAll` corresponds to the method in your Java Service. "
"This method returns a https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/"
"JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise[Promise] with the JsonRPC result."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "In this case, the result is an array, so we can loop over it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JsonArray (or any Java collection), either blocking or nonblocking, will "
"return an array; otherwise, a JsonObject will be returned."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/main/extensions/cache/deployment/"
"src/main/resources/dev-ui/qwc-cache-caches.js[Example code]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also pass in parameters in the method being called, for example:\n"
"(In the Runtime Java code)"
msgstr ""

msgid "The clear method takes one parameter called `name`"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the Webcomponent (Javascript):"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `name` parameter is passed in."
msgstr ""

msgid "Streaming data"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can keep a UI screen updated with the latest data by continuously "
"streaming data to the screen. This can be done with `Multi` (Java side) and "
"`Observer` (Javascript side)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Java side of streaming data:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Return the Multi that will stream jokes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/phillip-kruger/quarkus-jokes/blob/"
"f572ed6f949de0c0b8cbfa99d7389ab5168fea65/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/"
"jokes/runtime/JokesJsonRPCService.java#L37[Example code]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Javascript side of streaming data:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can call the method (optionally passing in parameters) and then provide "
"the code that will be called on the next event."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make sure to keep an instance of the observer to cancel later if needed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/phillip-kruger/quarkus-jokes/blob/main/deployment/src/"
"main/resources/dev-ui/qwc-jokes-web-components.js[Example code]"
msgstr ""

msgid "JsonRpc against the deployment classpath"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In certain cases you might need to execute methods and/or get data against "
"the deployment classpath. This also happens over JsonRPC communication, but "
"in this case you do not create a JsonRPC Service in the runtime module,\n"
"you can just supply the code to be run in a supplier in the deployment "
"module. To do this you will produce a `BuildTimeActionBuildItem`, example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Return or use a BuildProducer to create a `BuildTimeActionBuildItem`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`BuildTimeActionBuildItem` is automatically scoped with your extension "
"namespace"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Here we add an action, that is the same as a request-response method. The "
"method name (that can be called from js in the same way as any json-rpc "
"service) is `generateManifests`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also return a `CompletableFuture`/`CompletionStage` as an action, "
"and if you want to stream data you need to use `addSubscription` (rather "
"than `addAction`) and return a `Flow.Publisher`."
msgstr ""

